# Cross-platform parity (ios + android)

This monorepo ships the same product on **iOS** (`ios/`) and **Android** (`android/`).

## Rule
A behavior, API, analytics, or user-visible UI change in one platform **requires the matching change in the other**, or an explicit PR note explaining why parity is deferred.

Timing of the Android update is governed by `ios-first.mdc` (iOS first; port after iOS commit or explicit ask).

## Shared seams (keep names aligned)
NetworkClient → ImageProvider → ViewModel → UI + Coordinator + AnalyticsTimer + Errors

## Product contracts that must stay aligned
- NASA search: `description={day} {MonthName}` + `media_type=image` (English month names for the query)
- Client-side anniversary filter on `date_created` (month/day)
- Random pick from filtered set (fallback to all)
- Image URL: first containing `large` | `medium` | `original`
- `http` → `https` rewrite on asset URLs
- HTML entity decoding on title/description
- Firebase Analytics event `downloading` with param `duration_ms`
